<title>USA: Portland General Q3 net rises.</title>
<headline>Portland General Q3 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>PORTLAND, Ore. 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>PORTLAND GENERAL CORP. AND SUBSIDIARIES</p>
<p>						Three-Months Ended</p>
<p>						 Sep 30	(000's)</p>
<p>						   1996	  1995</p>
<p> Operating Revenues		    $260,091     $222,612</p>
<p> Operating Expenses		     196,665	161,529</p>
<p> Income Taxes				18,684	 20,817</p>
<p> Net Operating Income		    44,742	 40,266</p>
<p> Net Income				  20,541	 14,181</p>
<p>Average Common Shares</p>
<p>  Outstanding			  51,158,923   50,798,082</p>
<p>Earnings (Loss) Per</p>
<p>  Average Common Share		     0.40	   0.28</p>
<p> Dividends Declared Per Share	    0.32	   0.30</p>
<p> Retail Customers (End of Period)   661,482	643,835</p>
<p> Retail MWh Sales (Thousands)	   4,103	  4,095</p>
<p> Wholesale MWh Sales (Thousands)	2,913	    591</p>
<p>						  Nine-Months Ended</p>
<p>						  September (000's)</p>
<p>						   1996	  1995</p>
<p> Operating Revenues		    $794,097     $701,681</p>
<p> Operating Expenses		     551,281	493,174</p>
<p> Income Taxes				79,655	 71,509</p>
<p> Net Operating Income		   163,161	136,998</p>
<p>Regulatory Disallowances</p>
<p>  (Net of Tax)				    -     (49,567)</p>
<p> Net Income				 103,582	 44,630</p>
<p>Average Common Shares   Outstanding			  51,110,760   50,696,185</p>
<p> Earnings Per Average Common Share     2.03	   0.88</p>
<p> Dividends Declared Per Share	    0.96	   0.90</p>
<p> Retail Customers (End of Period)   661,482	643,835</p>
<p> Retail MWh Sales (Thousands)	  12,770	 12,576</p>
<p> Wholesale MWh Sales (Thousands)	7,152	  1,674</p>
<p>Note - Q3 1996 earnings include after-tax charges of $5 million for regulatory adjustments related to the company's energy efficiency programs and $5 million for merger related costs. Excluding these non-operating charges, earnings for the quarter would have been $31 million, or $0.61 per share.</p>
<p>Q3 1995 included a $13 million after-tax charge related to the company's deferred power cost filing. Excluding this item, earnings for the third quarter of 1995 would have been $27 million, or $0.53 per share.</p>
<p>Nine months 1995 results include regulatory disallowances of $50 million after tax related to the rate order disallowing 13 percent of the company's remaining investment in Trojan and the deferred power cost filing. Excluding these items, earnings for the nine months ended Sept. 30, 1995, period would have been $94 million, or $1.86 per share.</p>
